    "question_text": "Answer/Define the following : Retained placenta.",
    "is_high_yield": true,
    "Core_Anatomy": "Utero-placental interface (cotyledonary-caruncular attachment).",
    "Pathogenesis_Immediate": "Retained placenta is the failure to expel fetal membranes within 3 hours in mares or 12 hours in cows.",
    "Pathogenesis_Deep": "Uterine inertia (atony), inadequate proteolysis of collagen fibers holding cotyledons to caruncles, or calcium deficiency prevent postpartum membrane detachment.",
    "Why_Not": "Metritis is post-partum infection of the uterus, often a sequel to retained placenta, not the retention itself.",
    "Wow_Approach": "In mares, retained placenta is a critical emergency; it can cause fatal laminitis and metritis within 24 hours if not removed."
