    "subject": "Theriogenology",
    "topic": "Granular Posthitis",
    "marks": 5,
    "question_text": "Granular posthitis",
    "is_high_yield": true,
    "Core_Anatomy": "Preputial epithelium.",
    "Pathogenesis_Immediate": "Granular posthitis is an infectious disease of bulls characterized by the formation of painful, inflammatory lymphoid nodules on the preputial mucosa.",
    "Pathogenesis_Deep": "Commonly caused by Mycoplasma or Ureaplasma species, the pathogens colonize the preputial epithelium, triggering chronic mononuclear cell infiltration, subepithelial lymphoid hyperplasia (appearing as granules), and localized epithelial erosion.",
    "Why_Not": "Balanitis is inflammation of the glans penis, whereas posthitis is strictly inflammation of the preputial sheath.",
